  "body": "## What changed\nWith the WCS page's \"Pick markers in viewport\" armed, a click that misses the nine box markers now also takes the part's own corners (feature points) and round-edge centres (hole, boss, slot ends; the #692 opt-in `centres` kind). A corner queues the existing undoable `SetWcs` at the vertex's world position (`pick::align::vertex` made `pub`); a centre queues the existing `SetWcsCircle`. Markers keep priority; a click on nothing is left to the pick mode. The hint text names the new targets. Fork synced at v0.19.0 (process files at PV 63).\n\nNot stacked: touches `wcs_circle_pick.rs`, a new test file, one hint line in `wcs_page.rs` (#1684 edits `wcs_page.rs` too; different hunk), `pick/align.rs` visibility. No overlap with #1695 or #1209 hunks.\n\nMCP: `set_wcs_from_features` (Origin role: vertex id or circular-edge centre) and `set_wcs_circle_centre` already reach the same point set; no follow-up needed.\n\n## Tests\nPinned by `crates/ui/src/egui_app/wcs_part_point_tests.rs`: `a_click_on_a_part_corner_anchors_the_origin_there_and_undo_restores_it`, `a_click_on_a_boss_rim_centre_anchors_the_origin_on_it`, `with_the_markers_off_a_corner_click_does_not_move_the_origin`, `a_vertex_that_no_longer_resolves_is_refused_by_name_and_queues_nothing`. Mutation-checked: removing the hook, the vertex arm, the centre arm or the refusal stamp each turns a test red; file restored and cmp-identical. Quick gate (app + ui suites) green, clippy -D warnings on camcraft-ui and camcraft-app clean. No snapshot PNGs touched. Not exercised: batch gate, hover highlight of candidate points (not added; see decision file).\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThese captures show the shipping WCS page and GPU viewport after the same click.\nBefore uses parent `101d82f9` picker behavior and hint. After uses the reviewed\npicker and hint. The unused current `queue_vertex` helper remains in the before\ncapture harness only so the current test suite compiles.\n\nBoth scenes start at WCS origin (1, 2, 3), with bottom-level box markers and\n**Pick markers in viewport** armed. Before, the click selects the part and the\norigin stays at (1, 2, 3). After, the corner click places G54 at (20, 20, 40) and\nthe boss rim centre click places it at (0, 0, 40). The WCS fields and viewport\norigin triad show the result.\n\n| Target | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Part corner | ![Corner before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/4bfb4b5a599a805a992151cd9d60c23d1df1bb4c/docs/reviews/1710/corner-before.png) | ![Corner after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/4bfb4b5a599a805a992151cd9d60c23d1df1bb4c/docs/reviews/1710/corner-after.png) |\n| Boss rim centre | ![Centre before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/4bfb4b5a599a805a992151cd9d60c23d1df1bb4c/docs/reviews/1710/centre-before.png) | ![Centre after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/4bfb4b5a599a805a992151cd9d60c23d1df1bb4c/docs/reviews/1710/centre-after.png) |\n\nReproduction and provenance are in `docs/reviews/1710/README.md`. The ignored\n`review_1710_wcs_page_and_viewport_evidence` capture test asserts the clicked\norigin and visible WCS page before rendering. Reverting the picker makes that\npin fail. Restoring it makes the pin pass. No snapshot goldens changed.\n\nChangelog: WCS page marker pick also anchors the origin on a part's corners and on circle/slot centres (#1502)\nEffort: medium (no escalation)\nProcess change: no\n\nFixes #1502\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
